# PLAINTEXT SHAPE of gitea-actions-retention.sops.yaml - this example is NOT read by kustomize and holds
# no secret. It parses as YAML so it can be copied, edited and encrypted as-is.
#
# The Gitea PAT the gitea-actions-run-retention CronJob deletes old Actions runs with. Identity = the
# dedicated NON-ADMIN user `actions-retention`, member of org team `actions-retention` (unit Actions=write,
# all repos, nothing else). Deliberately not gitea_admin: write:repository on an admin is every repo.
#
# One-time setup (done 2026-09-28, ailab#923). Each command is one line; nothing after `--` is a comment.
#
# 1. the user (its password is never used and is discarded):
#      kubectl --context admin@ai -n gitea exec deploy/gitea -c gitea -- gitea admin user create --username actions-retention --email actions-retention@bots.local --random-password --must-change-password=false
#
# 2. the team, through the admin API with the gitea-admin break-glass basic auth (no admin PAT):
#      POST /api/v1/orgs/cchifor/teams
#        {"name":"actions-retention","permission":"write","units":["repo.actions"],
#         "units_map":{"repo.actions":"write"},"includes_all_repositories":true,"can_create_org_repo":false}
#      PUT  /api/v1/teams/<team id>/members/actions-retention
#    Proof of scope with the resulting token: GET /orgs/cchifor/repos 200, GET runs 200, DELETE of a
#    bogus run id 404 (permission passed), GET /repos/cchifor/platform/contents/README.md 403.
#
# 3. the token (PAT scopes are immutable; a wrong set means a new token). Never to the terminal:
#      kubectl --context admin@ai -n gitea exec deploy/gitea -c gitea -- gitea admin user generate-access-token -u actions-retention -t actions-run-retention --scopes read:organization,write:repository --raw > /some/mode-600/file
#    then, on the workstation with the age key (kubernetes/infra/_out/age.agekey, main checkout):
#      cp gitea-actions-retention.sops.yaml.example gitea-actions-retention.sops.yaml
#      (replace REPLACE_ME with the token in an editor - not via a shell command that lands in history)
#      sops --encrypt --in-place gitea-actions-retention.sops.yaml
#    `git diff` must show ENC[...] for `token` and nothing else in plaintext.
#    Rotate = repeat step 3 and delete the old token:
#      kubectl --context admin@ai -n gitea exec deploy/gitea -c gitea -- gitea admin user delete-access-token -u actions-retention -t actions-run-retention
apiVersion: v1
kind: Secret
metadata:
  name: gitea-actions-retention
  namespace: gitea
type: Opaque
stringData:
  token: REPLACE_ME
